inline juce::String storyEn()
{
    return juce::String::fromUTF8 (
        "In 1987, in a damp garage, an engineer nicknamed Jetty Gas was fixing an old tape "
        "deck and dropped a sprat sandwich straight into the circuit board. Instead of "
        "sparks, the speakers went boom-tss-boom-tss - backwards. That is how the world's "
        "first fish-powered beat slicer was born.\n\nBy 1991 the prototype weighed 14 "
        "kilograms, ate 400 watts and would only switch on with written permission from "
        "the cat. The spectral module was invented by accident: Jetty Gas tried to freeze "
        "dumplings with sound. The dumplings stayed warm, but they still sound "
        "great.\n\nLater the unit was lost during a house move and found in 2026 inside a "
        "washing machine, still running and producing an LFO at spin-cycle frequency. "
        "Jetty Gas said, \"Right, time to digitise this,\" and BM-900 now lives as a plugin. "
        "The screws are painted on, but very convincing.\n\nSide effects: a sudden urge to "
        "slice everything into 16 parts, addiction to the RANDOM button and a feeling that "
        "your monitors got warmer.\n\nTip: right-click any knob to assign an LFO to it. One "
        "LFO can drive as many parameters as you like - the machine only enjoys it.");
}

inline juce::String footEn()
{
    return juce::String::fromUTF8 (
        "The plugin is ABSOLUTELY FREE. Forever. No keys, no subscriptions, no sign-up. "
        "Jetty Gas refuses to take money on principle - only likes, shares with friends "
        "and kind words on Telegram.");
}

